	"descriptionMarkdown": "Im sure someone else enjoys space as much as I do!\n\nIts a non-recursive automall I designed that operates in space, because why not!\nIt keeps any recipe in memory for 1800 ticks (30seconds) and then voids, because it will assume that the item cannot be crafted.\nThere are 6 crafting cells to be faster. All assemblers are using \"prime offsets\" to not craft more than what is asked for.\n\nThe constant combinator left below the space hub holds all things that are meant to be crafted.\n\nKnown bugs: Sometimes assemblers dont work for a cycle, Im not sure why this is the case but since a cycle is no more than a few seconds this shouldnt be a big deal.\n\nSadly it is possible for the assemblers to become permanently stuck if the randomness of the selector combinator decides to always select the same output (albeit unliekly).\n\nThe mall selects new things to craft at random, and always requests the difference between what it has and what it would need from the planet / platforms.\n\nOpen to any suggestions. I am sure that this is significantly more complex than what it needs, especially the second assembler to obtain the crafting ingredients which I couldnt get around with surely has a neat solutoin I couldnt think of.\n\nI dont think that this should come into question, but if you decide to only use normal inserters instead of legendary ones you might need to adjust the 30second timer as its possible for a crafting recipe to need more than 30seconds to be filled by a regular inserter (think of nuclear reactors, they use a ton of items). In that case just increase the timer of the wasting system\n\nAnother noteworthy thing.. obviously this only crafts things with assemblers, so if you want to craft beacons / power poles / etc (things that could benefit from EM plants, foundries, etc) then dont include them in here. But I personally dont mind the \"wasted\" material for building stuff, so I didnt include a special crafting slot for those\n",
